 **Decision:** `GET /api/usage` summarizes this UTC month's rows (spend vs ceiling and state, by feature with blocked/failed counts and tokens, by model over calls that reached a provider, unknown-price models, the last 20 failed or blocked calls with codes). Sums are in micro-dollars. `/usage` renders it with a progress bar, a warn note, an alert when over, and "Costs are estimates from a built-in price table, not your Anthropic or Voyage invoice." The home page links to it; the link is a client component that fetches `/api/usage` and shows "N% of AI budget" (floored) at warn or "AI budget reached" when over, nothing otherwise — the home page is prerendered at build time, so a server-side query would have frozen build-time numbers into it. Feature names come from a map typed over `AI_OPERATIONS`, so a new operation without a label is a compile error. There is no global header, so the badge is on the home page only.
 **What it affects:** `apps/web/src/app/api/usage/route.ts`, `apps/web/src/lib/aiUsage/summarizeUsage.ts`, `apps/web/src/lib/aiUsage/format.ts`, `apps/web/src/app/usage/`, `apps/web/src/app/AiUsageLink.tsx`, `apps/web/src/app/page.tsx`.
 
+### D163. Phase 11a verification: a patch replay from main and a real-browser E2E on a synthetic user
+**Decision:** The plan's code was written and verified in a draft worktree, then replayed from `main` task by task as test/implementation patches: every task's tests failed before its implementation and passed after it, and `pnpm --filter web build`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` (0 warnings) and the forced full suite passed at every task's state (17/17 packages; 1851 tests after Task 1, 1974 after Task 11). The real-browser E2E (headless system Chrome via playwright-core) ran the built web app and the matching worker against `career_intel_test` as user `…0b06`, with the fake Anthropic server (now returning token usage: 200,000 in / 20,000 out = $0.30 per Haiku call), an invalid Voyage key and a local fake Langfuse OTLP receiver, under a $0.70 ceiling — 18 checks passed: empty start; a goal parse recorded and priced; the worker's match explanation recorded and Voyage 401s recorded as `voyage:401`; the warn band (`85% of AI budget` badge, warn note); a second parse taking spend over; a third parse blocked with the exact budget message in the goal form and a zero-cost `blocked` row; the "AI budget reached" badge and the blocked alert on `/usage`; one OTLP export per recorded call (6), all to `/api/public/otel/v1/traces` with basic auth and `x-langfuse-ingestion-version: 4`, none containing the goal text. The E2E user's rows were deleted afterwards.
+**Found by the E2E, not by unit tests:** Next.js renders its own empty `role="alert"` route announcer on every page, so a bare `getByRole("alert")` matched it instead of the budget alert (the check was narrowed by text; the component is unchanged). The fake Anthropic server returned no `usage` block, which would have made every E2E call look unpriced; it now returns configurable token counts.
+**What it affects:** `services/matching-worker/e2e/fakeAnthropic.ts`; the E2E kit in `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-07-phase-11a-ai-usage-cost-control/e2e/`.
+
 *Entries are appended chronologically. Do not edit or delete past entries when a decision is later reversed — add a new entry that supersedes it and cross-reference the original.*
